course: dictionary
lesson: 12260
title: Contamination: when something unwanted spoils
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Contamination means something has been made dirty, impure or harmful by something that should not be there. Look at the words around it for clues. «Contamination of the river made the fish ill.» The river was spoiled by something unwanted, and the fish became ill, so contamination means harmful spoiling.
explain: Kitchens have a special kind of contamination. «Use a separate knife for raw meat to stop cross-contamination of the salad.» Raw meat can carry germs, and they can spread to food that is eaten uncooked. Cross-contamination means germs moving from one thing to another.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The scientist threw away the sample because of contamination from dust.» If we swap in "because of spoiling by dust", the sentence still makes sense. Contamination is the spoiling, and dust is the unwanted material.
fact: Contamination means being made dirty, impure or harmful by something unwanted.
fact: «Contamination» is a noun that you cannot count, so we say "some contamination", not "a contamination".
fact: The verb is «contaminate», which means to make something dirty or harmful.
fact: In science, contamination is unwanted material that spoils a sample or an experiment.
fact: «Cross-contamination» in a kitchen means germs spreading from raw food to food that is eaten uncooked.
exercise: «Contamination of the river made the fish ill.» What does contamination mean here? | * Harmful spoiling by something unwanted | Clean water flowing fast | Fish swimming in groups | A big fishing competition
exercise: «Use a separate knife for raw meat to stop cross-contamination of the salad.» What does cross-contamination mean? | A knife made of shiny metal | * Germs spreading from raw food to other food | Salad that has been cooked for a long time | Cutting the salad into small pieces
exercise: «The scientist threw away the sample because of contamination from dust.» What was the unwanted material that spoiled the sample? | The cold lab | * Dust | A clean glass tube | Bright sunshine
test: «Clean water is important, so the town tested for contamination.» What was the town checking for? | Whether the water was cold | * Something harmful that spoils the water | The price of water | The name of the river
test: Mum says, «Wash the chopping board after raw chicken to avoid cross-contamination.» Why should you wash it? | To dry the wood in the sun | To make the board heavier | * To stop germs spreading to other food | To make the board look new
exam: «The air in the city had contamination from smoke, so people wore masks.» What does contamination suggest about the air? | The air had a sweet smell | The air was cool and fresh | The air was very quiet | * Harmful, unwanted things were in the air
